  "body": "Refs #979\nClaim: cloud/i817-sonnet\nAuthor model: sonnet-5.5 (cloud/i817-sonnet)\n\n### Problem\nOn the device, a tap on a section title in Favoris (« Apple », compact density, sectioned) freezes the app (#979). The cause is not established: the code path was read, never reproduced, and a hang cannot be captured from a Linux session.\n\n### Cause\nNot known yet. Read so far: the header button calls `NavigationModel.openCategory`, which writes `topicFilter.flag` and then `openedCategory`; the Favoris list models have no `topicFilter` (`supportsFlagFilter` is false), and the only compact-only code on the path is `DensityHeaderMargin` (`ListDensity.swift`). Neither is shown to loop.\n\n### Change\n**Test only, no fix.** `FavorisHeaderOpenHostedTests` hosts the Favoris `TopicsColumn` in a `NavigationStack` (two sections), in compact density and, as a control, in regular density. It does what the header's button does and expects the category list to be pushed (its topics requested) within `.timeLimit(.minutes(1))`. It logs to stderr after the `topicFilter` write, after `openedCategory` and after the push (`[#979] …` lines). A watchdog thread names the step and ends the run when the main thread is silent for 45 s.\n\nNot done: a real tap on the header's `Button` (a SwiftUI button has no UIKit handle in the hosted list); the test calls the same `openCategory` path. If it passes in both densities, the freeze needs the tap path or the device: ask the Mac for an Instruments trace.\n\n### Tests\nThe new test is the change. It must run on the macOS runner (ready PR); it was not run here (Linux), only SwiftLint `--strict` locally.\n\n### Next\ncloud/orch marks it ready alone on the runner and reads the log. If it hangs, the log names the step, the fix goes in this PR (`Refs` becomes `Closes #979`) with an Opus delta.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CGZzkXYrewmmsp8fYF)_",
